Diagnostic — what is wired vs. what api-base.ts requires
--------------------------------------------------------
api-base.ts line 36-46 builds URLs as:
    `${origin}/${worker}` when NEXT_PUBLIC_API_ORIGIN is set
i.e. https://forge.echo-op.com/ept-api/...
     https://forge.echo-op.com/daedalus-forge/...
     etc., for ~30 workers referenced across lib/.

D33.5 actually ships only:
  forge.echo-op.com/sdk/*  -> echo-workers.service SDK gate (151 caps, OK)
  forge.echo-op.com/health -> health endpoint (OK)
Everything else returns 404 or hangs (curl timeout):
  /ept-api/         -> 404 in 36ms
  /daedalus-forge/  -> connection timeout 6s
  /sentinel-cloud/  -> connection timeout 6s
  /knowledge-api/   -> 404
  /pipeline-api/    -> connection timeout 6s
  /stripe-api/      -> connection timeout 6s

Per-worker subdomain alternative also unavailable:
  ept-api.echo-op.com         -> NXDOMAIN (no A record)
  daedalus-forge.echo-op.com  -> NXDOMAIN
  sentinel-cloud.echo-op.com  -> NXDOMAIN

Why this is a real blocker, not a defect on D33.5
-------------------------------------------------
D33.5 was scoped to "named cloudflared tunnel" + SDK gate publication, and
that shipped correctly. D33.4b assumed "tunnel = full worker mesh on
forge.echo-op.com" but the worker reverse-proxy directives in Caddy were
never written (or the workers themselves still live on Cloudflare and
were not ported to FORGE). Either way the path-prefix routing convention
named in api-base.ts is unimplemented.

Flipping NEXT_PUBLIC_API_ORIGIN=https://forge.echo-op.com right now would
break every non-SDK fetch on echo-prime-tech.com production. Code-prep
from D33.4 is correct and stays in place; the env override stays
commented out.

